  "full_text": "Yeah, there was Dave the bartender in the dorm. Used to get like a shopping cart full of liquor for the dorm. He's a Russian. We used to, he had a big laugh. Anyway, then there was Boris at Ticketmaster. He was, Cal was the electrical engineer, Iranian guy. Anyway, and his assistant was Boris. He did the like board layout and stuff and like he was kind of like how do I put this? I had a strange kind of competence Like he's an Iranian like he's not exactly the most Impressive I don't think he can solve math problems in electrical engineering, but he gets his shit done, right? He's got a lot of wisdom and stuff like that Boris is kind of I think he had a master's degree in electrical engineering. He's kind of like Igor from Frankenstein. A little bit. The relationship, kind of like, they talk all the time and they're both kind of, how do I put it? They come off as being kind of like, let's just say like, not exactly MIT people, but somehow both of them together get it done. And then he had, Cal told a story about in Iran. There was a river that he went to the radio station. They had tubes, you know, vacuum tubes. Apparently for the transmitter, they had a huge vacuum tube. He said they used to have a river that cooled it, like they ran a river in or something. And he said he was hooked or something, I don't know. But anyway, so like, then there was, I think Alex, there was a young Russian guy that... that came over and he worked in the, he assembled ticket printers. I think he was probably underemployed, you know. He was young. I don't know how to, and then there was, yeah. I'm trying to mimic the, you know, the lots of emotion and whatever. Anyway, so then there was, who else was there? Oh, well, oh.",
